Algorithm 1  Spam Detection Classification Procedure

Require: Input message M, Trained pipeline P (TF-IDF Vectorizer + MNB Classifier),
         Confidence threshold θ (default = 0.7)
Ensure:  Classification result R with label, confidence score, and risk level

 1:  function CLASSIFY_SPAM(M, P, θ)
 2:      T ← ConvertToLowercase(M)
 3:      T ← RemovePunctuation(T)
 4:      T ← RemoveSpecialCharacters(T)
 5:      tokens ← Tokenize(T)
 6:      tokens ← RemoveStopWords(tokens)
 7:      tokens ← ApplyStemming(tokens)
 8:      T_processed ← JoinTokens(tokens)
 9:      V ← TF-IDF_Transform(T_processed, P.vectorizer)
10:      P_spam ← P.classifier.predict_proba(V)[spam]
11:      P_ham  ← P.classifier.predict_proba(V)[ham]
12:      confidence ← max(P_spam, P_ham)
13:      if P_spam > P_ham then
14:          label ← "SPAM"
15:      else
16:          label ← "HAM"
17:      end if
18:      if label = "SPAM" and confidence ≥ θ then
19:          if confidence ≥ 0.9 then
20:              risk_level ← "CRITICAL"
21:          else if confidence ≥ 0.8 then
22:              risk_level ← "HIGH"
23:          else
24:              risk_level ← "MEDIUM"
25:          end if
26:          GenerateAlert(label, confidence, risk_level)
27:      else if label = "SPAM" and confidence < θ then
28:          risk_level ← "LOW"
29:          LogAsLowConfidence(label, confidence)
30:      else
31:          risk_level ← "NONE"
32:      end if
33:      R ← {label, confidence, risk_level}
34:      return R
35:  end function